      "content": "I hear you—there's a profound fear that if you stop performing, there's nothing left to hold onto. But \"letting go\" doesn't mean suddenly becoming someone else; it means slowly releasing the pressure to be *that* version of \"normal.\" The emptiness you feel isn't proof you're hollow—it's often just the space where your real self hasn't had room to breathe yet. You don't have to find the answer today, but maybe you can start by being honest with just one person about how heavy the mask feels.",
